          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Figure it Out"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.292,
            0.77,
            0.385
          ],
          "content": "1. Circle the following statements of proportion that are true. (i) 4 : 7 :: 12 : 21 (ii) 8 : 3 :: 24 : 6 (iii) 7 : 12 :: 12 : 7 (iv) 21 : 6 :: 35 : 10 (v) 12 : 18 :: 28 : 12 (vi) 24 : 8 :: 9 : 3"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.39,
            0.441,
            0.411
          ],
          "content": "**Ans.** (i), (iv) and (vi) are true."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.426,
            0.609,
            0.467
          ],
          "content": "2. Give 3 ratios that are proportional to 4 : 9."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.473,
            0.601,
            0.59
          ],
          "content": "**Ans.** Given ratio is 4 : 9 3 ratios that are proportional of 4 : 9 are 49 × 2 4 × 33 and $\\frac{4}{9} \\times \\frac{4}{4}$ 2, 9 Or, 8:18, 12:27 and 16:36 Try for more."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.598,
            0.846,
            0.66
          ],
          "content": "3. Fill in the missing numbers for these ratios that are proportional to 18 : 24. 3 : 12 : 20 : 27 :"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.664,
            0.318,
            0.798
          ],
          "content": "**Ans.** (i) 3 : 4 (ii) 12 : 16 (iii) $2 0 : \\frac { 8 0 } { 3 }$ (iv) 27 : 36"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.806,
            0.847,
            0.865
          ],
          "content": "4. Look at the following rectangles. Which rectangles are similar to each other? You can verify this by measuring the width and height using a scale and comparing their ratios."
